,d$b.   THE STORY OF EARTHBOUND ZERO                                     ,d$b.
$$  '                                                                    `  $$
`qb        I've told this story so many times to so many people already,   qb'
,d$b.      one  last time  won't hurt.  What you're  playing  here  is a ,d$b.
`  $$      prototype ROM  -  the holy grail as far as unofficial hacking $$  '
  qb'      and translating goes. What happened  with EarthBound Zero was `qb
,d$b.      that Nintendo of America had it translated  from japanese and ,d$b.
$$  '      everything, but somewhere along the way, scrapped the funding `  $$
`qb        for  a public release.  So what are you left with?  Prototype   qb'
,d$b.      carts! an instant rarity as |tsr would say.                   ,d$b.
`  $$                                                                    $$  '
  qb'      Anyhow,  some  guy by  the name of  Mariotti obtained  one of `qb
,d$b.      these Prototype carts from a  mysterious source from Nintendo ,d$b.
$$  '      of America  and was auctioning  it off in mid-January,  1998. `  $$
`qb        Someone  let the  translation  community know  about it on my   qb'
,d$b.      wwwboard  a few days later.  since i was planning on doing an ,d$b.
`  $$      unofficial  translation hack  of it myself  (like we did with $$  '
  qb'      final fantasy 2j), this was indeed very kewl to hear.         `qb
,d$b.                                                                    ,d$b.
$$  '      Alas,  the cart had already been sold by the time i could get `  $$
`qb        ahold of the guy. This is where the story takes a wierd turn.   qb'
,d$b.      After a month or so, we finally managed to find out the email ,d$b.
`  $$      address of the guy who bought the prototype cart.  A deal was $$  '
  qb'      struck for 400 (!$@#!@#$) dollars to be able to dump the ROM, `qb
,d$b.      200 up front and 200 when the dump was successful. Apparently ,d$b.
$$  '      this guy was  concerned about the  depreciation of the cart's `  $$
`qb        value,  since once dumped,  it would no  longer be a one of a   qb'
,d$b.      kind item.                                                    ,d$b.
`  $$                                                                    $$  '
  qb'      After  weeks of begging,  sobbing,  as well as a  good bit of `qb
,d$b.      criticism by  the people  who thought  it was all a sham,  we ,d$b.
$$  '      finally got enough money together to actually go through with `  $$
`qb        this. So, the cash was mailed on 4/22/98,  the buyer sent the   qb'
,d$b.      cart on 4/25, and the ROM was dumped, hacked, and released on ,d$b.
`  $$      4/27.                                                         $$  '
  qb'                                                                    `qb
,d$b.      The ROM required a moderate amount of hacking in order to get ,d$b.
$$  '      it running well with popular NES emulators  (NESticle). Orig- `  $$
`qb        inally, there  was a bug with  the text display,  so TrelaneQ   qb'
,d$b.      did a little job with the coding  (only one byte was actually ,d$b.
`  $$      changed) to get it to  display text without  locking up. How- $$  '
  qb'      ever, as the public  played through the game  with this newly `qb
,d$b.      released hack, at two crucial points in the game we got these ,d$b.
$$  '      illegal screen  messages telling  us that  our  ROM had  been `  $$
`qb        tampered with and that it would  no longer function. This was   qb'
,d$b.      a result of TrelaneQ's hacking the ROM,  so Barubary (another ,d$b.
`  $$      ROM hacker -  he did the ff5  translation)  and TrelaneQ went $$  '
  qb'      back  into the ROM  to nullify the  self-checking  code which `qb
,d$b.      made  the game jump to  the illegal screen.  After that,  the ,d$b.
$$  '      game was fully playable.  If you'd like the original ROM like `  $$
`qb        it  was when  dumped from  its cart,  visit the  NDF homepage   qb'
,d$b.      (listed below). It won't work on NESticle very well, but i've ,d$b.
`  $$      heard it'll play fine on FCE Linux and DarkNESs for Amiga.    $$  '
  qb'                                                                    `qb
,d$b.      To all of you who helped, i know i can't thank each and every ,d$b.
$$  '      one of you personally,  but just let me say thanks. Thank you `  $$
`qb        so much for  firstly having  the balls to invest in something   qb'
,d$b.      as shaky as  this and helping  not only the  series of Mother ,d$b.
`  $$      to live on  but also the  universal trust  of people like us. $$  '
  qb'      To all the doubters,  cynics,  and especially  those who just `qb
,d$b.      sat back and let someone else flip the bill, fuck you.        ,d$b.
$$  '                                                                    `  $$
